@startuml Communication Diagram
title Communication Diagram - Inter-Task Communication via FreeRTOS Primitives

rectangle "vTaskDetect\n(Priority 3)" as detect #LightBlue
rectangle "vTaskDisplay\n(Priority 2)" as display #LightGreen
rectangle "vTaskLED\n(Priority 1)" as ledtask #LightYellow

database "SharedData" as shared #LightGray {
    card "press_duration : uint32_t"
    card "new_press_detected : bool"
    card "button_pressed : bool"
    card "task_state : uint8_t"
}

hexagon "semPressDisplay" as spd #Orange
hexagon "semReleaseDisplay" as srd #Orange
hexagon "semPressLED" as spl #Orange
hexagon "semReleaseLED" as srl #Orange
hexagon "lcdMutex" as lm #Red

rectangle "Joystick" as joy #Wheat
rectangle "LcdI2c" as lcd #Wheat
rectangle "Led R/G/Y" as leds #Wheat

' Detect task interactions
detect --> joy : 1. scan()
detect --> shared : 2. write state
detect --> spd : 3a. give() on press
detect --> spl : 3b. give() on press
detect --> srd : 4a. give() on release
detect --> srl : 4b. give() on release

' Display task interactions
spd --> display : 5a. take() - press event
srd --> display : 5b. take() - release event
display --> lm : 6. take()/give()
display --> lcd : 7. updateLCD()
display --> shared : 8. read duration\n& write task_state

' LED task interactions
spl --> ledtask : 9a. take() - press event
srl --> ledtask : 9b. take() - release event
ledtask --> leds : 10. on()/off()
ledtask --> shared : 11. read duration\n& task_state

note bottom of spd
  **Binary Semaphores** are used
  for event signaling between tasks.
  
  Press events: semPressDisplay + semPressLED
  Release events: semReleaseDisplay + semReleaseLED
end note

note bottom of lm
  **Mutex** protects
  LCD I2C bus access
  from concurrent writes
end note

note right of shared
  **Shared memory** is accessed
  by all three tasks.
  Written by Detect,
  read by Display & LED.
end note

@enduml
